From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Feb 28 20:12:32 2002
From: Greg Freemyer <freemyer () NorcrossGroup ! com>
Date: Thu, 28 Feb 2002 20:12:32 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary Update: Automating HSG-80 snapshots without using EVM.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622501


I just got in an e-mail from Han Pilmeyer.

Han informs me that there is a best practice related to this topic at =
http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/docs/best_practices/BP_SNAPSHOT/TITLE.HTM

He also says that the process can get tricky because you have to know which =
HSG-80 is serving the data set and issue your commands to that HSG.

=3D=3D=3D=3D First Summary

I got 3 responses, all saying to check out "Command Scripter".

Thanks to:
 Joe Carrico
 Kris Chandrasekhar
 Allen Carpenter

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D Orig. quistion
=20
I need to create a HSG-80 based snapshot everyday for auditing purposes.

I'm familiar with the various ACS versions, and with using EVM to manage the =
snapshot process.  (I have only created a snapshot via EVM, never manually, so =
the below may be way off base.)

I just priced EVM 2.0 and the management appliance it requires to run on.  =
$25K.

That seems pretty expensive for what I assume can be done using cron and some =
kind of script.

At worst I assume I could connect a serial connection from the Alpha to the =
HSG-80 and use an Expect script to create the snapshot under cron's control, =
then mount it and start a separate instance of the database.

Is that logical, or is there a better way to automate this process.  (I have a =
DBA that can figure out the database part.  I just need to create and mount the =
snapshot.)

Thanks,
Greg Freemyer
Internet Engineer
Deployment and Integration Specialist
The Norcross Group
www.NorcrossGroup.com



