From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Feb 28 02:26:13 2002
From: "Arjen Visser \(DSL AK\)" <ArjenV () datacom ! co ! nz>
Date: Thu, 28 Feb 2002 02:26:13 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Will relabeling disk destroy exisiting partitions on sam	e
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622472

Relabeling the partions will not destroy exisiting partitions on the same
disk.

You will need to make sure that the system isn't actually using it as swap.
- Check the fstab and the partition(s) pointed to by the sysconfig file
(5.x)
  or by /sbin/swapdefault
- You will need to reboot to clear the swap usage.

Once you've done that, just use "mkfdmn" to make the file domain, or
if you want to add the space to an existing volume, "addvol", and the
AdvFS software will change the partition use ("fstype") to AdvFS.

Thanks for all the answers, 
Arjen

