Dear Tru64 managers,

My earlier summary of the resolution to my problem with compatibility
of DLT8000 tapes/drives with SGI machines was incomplete:

The stanza that I needed to add to /var/sysgen/master.d/scsi (just
after the one defining the DLT7000) is:

	/* DEC THZxx DLT drive */
        { DECDLT, TPDLT, 0, 7, "", "DLT8000", 0, 0,
          {0x1B /*7000*/, 0x1B /*7000c*/, 0x1A /*4000*/, 0x1A /*4000c*/ },
          MTCAN_BSF|MTCAN_BSR|MTCAN_APPEND|MTCAN_SPEOD |
            MTCAN_CHKRDY|MTCAN_VAR| MTCAN_SETSZ|MTCAN_SILI|MTCAN_SEEK|
              MTCAN_SYNC|MTCAN_CHTYPEANY|MTCAN_COMPRESS|MTCAN_SETDEN,
          20, 8*60, 20*60, 5*60, 3*3600, 4096, 64*1024,
          tpsc_dlt7000_dens_count, tpsc_dlt7000_hwg_dens_names,tpsc_dlt7000_alias_dens_names,
          {0}, 0, 0, 0,
          0, (u_char *)0 },


Andrew

