From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Feb 22 16:47:03 2002
From: "Karen R. McArthur" <kmcarthu () bates ! edu>
Date: Fri, 22 Feb 2002 16:47:03 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Problems with Rolling Upgrade
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622382

I love this list!
Thanks to Pat O'Brien, Vincent D'Antonio, Paul LaMadeleine, Han Pilmeyer,
Chris Ford, Phil Baldwin, Dr Thomas Blinn, Timothy Brown, Scott Fafrak,
Jason Orendorf, Howard Arnold and "Travis" at Compaq Support.

We've figured out the issues around our Rolling Upgrade problem.

Summary of problem:
"clu_upgrade -v check setup 1" came back with an error that some members
appeared to be running with tagged files
"clu_upgrade clean" came back with a previous stage hasn't completed or
clean has already been run
"clu_upgrade status" came back with the members appearing to be in single
user mode or in the process of a boot (even though both nodes are up and
functional)
"sysconfig -h <node>-mc0 -s generic" came back with "framework error:
connection problems"

Resolution:
The problem ended up being 3-fold:
1.) there was a typo in our /.rhosts file
2.) cfgmgr was commented out in inetd.conf
3.) cfgmgr was within a tcpwrapper

I fixed these issues, ran HUP on inetd (on both nodes), and our clu_upgrade
appears to be working.
Thanks again!
--
