From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Feb 19 17:19:04 2002
From: Dave Love <d.love () dl ! ac ! uk>
Date: Tue, 19 Feb 2002 17:19:04 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] Re: single sign-on with normal KDC
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622323

I wrote:

> Will the SSO stuff in 5.1a authenticate against a non-Microshafted
> KDC, i.e. MIT or Heimdal?  If so, is any magic required?

Sometime later, I got information from Tom Sweeney at Compaq.

It turns out you can get tickets vanilla KDC iff you specify the
encryption type as `des-crc', i.e. `kinit -e des-crc ...'.  You can't
currently use the SSO stuff to build Kerberized net apps, though it
`should' be possible.  Kerberized services are apparently in the works
for a future release.

I'll stick to Heimdal for now.

