Subject: Busted cron
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622320

I've got a rather bizarre problem on a Tru65 4.0D box. Cron is busted
for a particular user and I'm not sure why. Here's the entry for the
user staffdb:

# Crontab for staffdb
#
55 5 * * * /usr/users/staffdb/staff_directory.php3 > cron.log 2>&1

The script FTPs a file to another machine and over the weekend I got a
complaint from that machine's admin that he was getting the file every
five minutes.

I made various changes to both the above entry and to the script to
verify that it was that script and that cron was running it. Originally
I thought there must be another script or that it was stuck in a loop.

None of that helped so I removed the entire file (crontab -r staffdb)
and re-created it. That helped somewhat. After that the script would run
at 51 minutes past the hour every hour. No idea why 51 except that it
