As we had these messages (although for single disks) we got these as
information that the disk controler or the on disk logic had discovered a
malfunctioning block in the disk surface and is going to set pointers to not
deal with this block anymore in the future. During disk foramtiing there are
bad block nearly every time, but the manufacturer-badblock-list holds the
&quot;personality of your individual disk&quot;. In addition to that, there=
 is
an amount of blocks reserved to do this &quot;bad block replacement&quot; o=
n the
fly, thus extending the bad block list. If it is exhausted data loss may oc=
cur.
Please do observe BBRs; if this number is increasing, replace the disk. If =
you
use AdvFS consider a rmvol/addvol.</span></font></p>

