Hello Managers,

One of my systems is an XP1000 running Tru64 5.0. This morning I have
planned to upgrade it to 5.1a going through 5.0a.

Some strange things happened during the first attempt of the upgrade as
removal of /sbin/sh and /shlib/libc.so, but I've restored them and
started the upgrade again.

The upgrade seemed to be OK till the reboot.

Then I have some 55 messages as

ERROR wrong cdev /dev/disk/xxx is 1300016 sb 1300008
bcheckrc Device Naming failed boot configure or verify.

I've removed the files and issued a dsfmgr -K command but the result is
the same.

In single user the bcheckrc command gives :

# bcheckrc
Checking device naming:
    Duplicate Local entry: A:  4efffff  4efffff       50       11
0   c
/dev/_scsi_scsi
