From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Feb 18 14:45:53 2002
From: jreed () athena ! appliedtheory ! com
Date: Mon, 18 Feb 2002 14:45:53 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: non-executable stack in 5.1a?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622292

Thanks to Martin Moore and Jan Mark Holzer for quick replies.
The non-executable stack is configured by default in (at least) 5.1a.
It is set with an option configurable via sysconfig:

vm:
	executable_stack = 0 (disallowed)

There is info in the man page for sys_attrs_proc. 

I do not know the status of this parameter in 5.0*. 

Thanks very much, 

Judith Reed

