From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Feb 15 14:00:40 2002
From: Mici Arnold <arnold.mici () theIMO ! com>
Date: Fri, 15 Feb 2002 14:00:40 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY - C2 settings in Tru64
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622258

MY QUESTION WAS:


Why when I try to change the setting in the field u_maxtries for a specific
user (using dxaccounts and edauth), the system is still using the settings
from the default file (/etc/auth/system/default) ?


ANSWER IS: (thank you ann.majeske@compaq)

It looks like what is happening is that the login command will cycle 5 times
requesting username/password
before it quits.  It does this regardless of the value of u_maxtries in the
user's account or the default database.
But, the user's account is really locked after the second attempt to enter a
bad password, so if on the third time
around I enter the right password, I get the "Account is disabled -- see
Account Administrator" message.

Regards

Arnold

