From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Feb 12 04:38:57 2002
From: "Neil McCoy" <Neil.McCoy () afp ! gov ! au>
Date: Tue, 12 Feb 2002 04:38:57 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: disklabel issues discussion
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622196


The following is FYI only

I have repeatedly had the disklabel issue that Xavier has had plus
others,
(running on a 2xGS60E cluster running 5.1 + patch kit 3)
including:

(i)   error 1024 on reading &/or writing a disklabel
(ii)   disklabel command hanging and not killable

COMPAQ Australia BCS currently reports no solution is available.

Our only workaround so far has been to:
(i) disable LSM permanently, ie. revert to h/w RAID
(ii) reboot anything from the node the command is running on up to a
full cluster reboot.

COMPAQ Australia BCS stats that running hwmgr scans, disklabel in the
wrong order
can cause the problem to occur.

My experience suggests that o minimise the problem use the following
procedure:

If the disk is a h/w storage set, wait until it finishes constructing
before scanning it.

Run 'hwmgr -scan scsi' sequentially one node at a time on each and
every cluster node.
( suggestion:  to monitor hwmgr progress, in another window on same
node run:   evmwatch -A -t "@timestamp  [@priority]   @name  @@"   )

Only after the scan is run on ALL nodes, create the disklabel,
preferably on the last node scanned.




