From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Feb 07 00:56:34 2002
From: Kid Rock <metatron8_8008 () yahoo ! com>
Date: Thu, 07 Feb 2002 00:56:34 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Auth database in 2-node cluster?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622127

Thank you for the quick responses, which I have below.

The summary is that in Tru64 v5.0 and later, the auth
database is shared between cluster members. A password
change on one affects all cluster members.


From: "Michael James Bradford" <mjbr@tdc.dk> 
 
To: "'Kid Rock'" <metatron8_8008@yahoo.com> 
 
Subject: SV: UPDATE: Auth database in 2 node cluster 
 
Date: Wed, 6 Feb 2002 22:11:43 +0100  
 

Hi there,

A password change on one node works for all nodes in a
TruCluster 
version 5
and later. That's one of the features.

Regards

Michael
--

From: "Ann Majeske" <Ann.Majeske@Compaq.com> 
 
To: "Kid Rock" <metatron8_8008@yahoo.com> 
 
Subject: Re: Auth database in 2-node cluster? 
 
Depends on the version you're running.
If you're running tru64 Version 5 or greater
the auth database is shared.  If you're running
a V4.* version you and you want to share the
auth database you have to do it with NIS
or NFS.

Ann


 
